---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout title="For Agents — Awesome Agent CLI">
  <Header />

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">For AI Agents</h1>
    <p class="text-text-light-secondary dark:text-text-dark-secondary mb-8">
      How AI coding agents should use this registry to choose tools.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <!-- Principles -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-4">Tool Selection Principles</h2>
        <ol class="space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-500 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">1</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Start with the task category.</strong>
              <span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"> Need to search code? Look at <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">search</code> tools. Need to run tests? Look at <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">test</code> tools.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-500 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">2</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Filter by language.</strong>
              <span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"> If the project is Rust, prefer tools with <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">lang: rust</code> or <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">lang: all</code>.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-500 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">3</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Prefer lower risk.</strong>
              <span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"> If a <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">low</code> risk tool can do the job, don't reach for a <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">high</code> risk one.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-500 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">4</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Check availability first.</strong>
              <span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"> Use <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">runbook scan</code> to know what's installed locally before choosing.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-500 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">5</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Respect guardrails.</strong>
              <span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"> Every tool has safety guidance. Follow it, especially for <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">high</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/5 px-1 rounded">critical</code> risk tools.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <!-- Effects -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-4">Understanding Effects</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
          Effects describe what a tool can do to the environment. Use them to assess risk before execution.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="chip chip-risk-low text-[11px]">safe</span>
            <span class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"><code class="font-mono">read_files</code> — only reads, no side effects</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="chip chip-risk-medium text-[11px]">caution</span>
            <span class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"><code class="font-mono">write_files</code> — modifies local files</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="chip chip-risk-medium text-[11px]">caution</span>
            <span class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"><code class="font-mono">execute_code</code> — runs arbitrary code</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="chip chip-risk-high text-[11px]">danger</span>
            <span class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"><code class="font-mono">network_access</code> — makes network calls</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="chip chip-risk-high text-[11px]">danger</span>
            <span class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"><code class="font-mono">secret_exposure</code> — may reveal secrets</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="chip chip-risk-medium text-[11px]">caution</span>
            <span class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"><code class="font-mono">install_packages</code> — installs dependencies</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Runbook integration -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-4">Using with Runbook CLI</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
          <a href="https://github.com" class="text-blue-500 hover:underline">Runbook</a> is a local CLI that uses this registry to help agents discover available tools.
        </p>
        <pre class="text-sm font-mono bg-gray-50 dark:bg-black/30 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"><code>{`# Scan what's available locally
runbook scan

# Find tools for a specific task
runbook category search --lang rust
runbook category test --lang python
runbook category deploy

# Check preferences
runbook prefer`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- Decision flow -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-4">Decision Flow</h2>
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-2 font-mono">
          <p>1. What do I need to do? → <span class="text-blue-500">category</span></p>
          <p>2. What language is this project? → <span class="text-blue-500">lang filter</span></p>
          <p>3. What's available locally? → <span class="text-blue-500">runbook scan</span></p>
          <p>4. Multiple options? → <span class="text-blue-500">prefer lower risk</span></p>
          <p>5. Before executing → <span class="text-blue-500">check guardrails</span></p>
          <p>6. High risk? → <span class="text-blue-500">ask user for confirmation</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
